depends messagemix
send 1
a1 sort (arrival) utf8 all
receive 2
* SORT 2 1 3
a1 OK done
send 1
a2 sort (cc) utf8 all
receive 2
* SORT 1 2 3
a2 OK done
send 1
a21 sort (cc arrival) utf8 all
receive 2
* SORT 2 1 3
a21 OK done
send 1
a3 sort (date) utf8 all
receive 2
* SORT 2 1 3
a3 OK done
send 1
a4 sort (from) utf8 all
receive 2
* SORT 1 2 3
a4 OK done
send 1
a5 sort (size) utf8 all
receive 2
* SORT 2 1 3
a5 OK done
send 1
a6 sort (subject) utf8 all
receive 2
* SORT 1 3 2
a6 OK done
send 1
a7 sort (to) utf8 all
receive 2
* SORT 1 2 3
a7 OK done
# 'reverse to' should make no difference at all, since the implicit
# uid sort is what actually orders the messages
send 1
a7b sort (reverse to) utf8 all
receive 2
* SORT 1 2 3
a7b OK done
# but reverse subject should matter
send 1
a6b sort (reverse subject) utf8 all
receive 2
* SORT 2 3 1
a6b OK done
# and the combination should work
send 1
a6c sort (to reverse subject) utf8 all
receive 2
* SORT 2 3 1
a6c OK done
send 1
a6d sort (subject) utf8 from <arnt@
receive 2
* SORT 1 3 2
a6d OK done
send 1
a8 sort (from) utf8 1:2
receive 2
* SORT 1 2
a8 OK done
end
